# backend/data is ~12GB on the machine this was built on, and almost none of it
# is read while SERVING. Everything the running app needs is either in Postgres
# (DATABASE_URL) or a hosted vector store (QDRANT_URL); what is left below is
# read-only book material the /assets mount serves.
data/*
!data/figure_knowledge
!data/figure_knowledge/**

# data/assets is 139MB of PAGE IMAGES extracted from the Cambridge books
# (p001_i0.png and friends, books 1-4 and 18). Reading them on this machine is
# personal use; serving them from a public URL is republishing someone else's
# book. They stay out, which also keeps the bundle small. The Cambridge TEXT is
# in Postgres and unaffected, and generated figures are drawn client-side from
# the `visual` JSON, so no practice material depends on this directory.

# 🚨 The source corpus. `books/` is 2.2GB of Cambridge PDFs and `Audios/` is
# the recordings that go with them — the copyrighted material that GROUNDS
# generation and must never be served. Nothing in app/ opens either while
# serving; the knowledge base built from them lives in Qdrant.
books/
Audios/

# Never needed at runtime.
tests/
tools/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
.env.*
